The hidden, opt-in `dafny verify --batch-gc` option runs verification with background garbage collection disabled from process startup. It can improve throughput on allocation-heavy projects, at the cost of responsiveness during collections. The command-line executable launches a child with the same arguments and runtime, forwards its standard streams and exit code, and waits for cleanup. Project configuration is supported; in-process verification APIs reject the option. Generated obligations and solver options are unchanged.
